+- **Breadcrumb filter widened + DEBUG drop-reason log added.** `IntegrationActivityProcessor.ShouldEmitActivityBreadcrumb` now accepts the Redis source only when the parent chain reaches a Memories or AspNetCore ancestor (walked up to depth 16, cycle-protected). Drops emit a DEBUG log entry with `reason ∈ { orphan_no_parent, parent_chain_not_reachable, depth_exceeded_16 }` so operators can triage "why didn't my Redis span show up?" without code spelunking. Pinned by `IntegrationActivityProcessorBreadcrumbFilterTests` (7 tests). The class was changed from `private sealed class` to `internal sealed class` and `InternalsVisibleTo` added to `Hexalith.Memories.Server.Tests` + `Hexalith.Memories.IntegrationTests` to make the member accessible to test code.
+- **Instrumentation Inventory parity test.** Task 4.3's root-cause mitigation for "aspirational spec, no auditor" pattern. `docs/dev/telemetry.md` gains a new "Instrumentation Inventory" section with a table listing every subscribed `ActivitySource.Name` + registration site + Tier-2 test. `InstrumentationInventoryTests.InventoryTable_MatchesRegisteredActivitySources` parses the table on every build and asserts each documented source is subscribed by the TracerProvider built via `AddServiceDefaults`. The next gap fails a unit test instead of a Tier-3 assertion six months after ship.
+- **AC #2 hard assertion wired through the existing stderr breadcrumb path.** The Redis spans flow through the same `IntegrationActivityProcessor` stderr breadcrumb path that Story 8.4 proved; `AspireEndToEndTraceTests.AssertRedisSpanInTraceAsync` uses `ServerActivityStreamReader.ReadAsync` with a `matchPredicate` filtering to the Redis source name + matching `TraceId`. The new `TelemetryAsserts.WaitForActivityAsync<T>` helper from Task 3.1.1 is shipped as infrastructure for future in-process Redis-span assertions but is not invoked by the current AC #2 assertion (the stderr reader's own poll loop handles the drain-thread cadence).
+- **Skip helpers deleted.** `Ac2RedisSkipReviewBy.cs` + `Ac2SkipReviewByTests.cs` removed from the repo. No `telemetry.redis.instrumentation.skipped` log-line emission remained in code — the string appears only in a retired-marker XML-doc comment in `AspireEndToEndTraceTests.cs` explaining the Story 8.5 retirement.
+- **Story 8.4 amendment.** The Story 8.5 workspace still stages the AC #2 hard-assertion flip, but the Story 8.4 artifact is now careful not to claim merge-commit / nightly evidence early. GitHub issue #9 is already closed by user; merge-backlink wording stays deferred until Story 8.5 actually lands on main.
 
